From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: foxnne <foxnne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:37:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] test: a fizzy suite for the Wayland driver on an older
 libxkbcommon

testautomation_fizzy_xkb.c checks that SDL's Wayland driver loads, and
builds its keymap's modifier levels right, wherever libxkbcommon is
older than the headers SDL was built against.

xkb_waylandDriverLoads restarts the video subsystem with the Wayland
driver whenever WAYLAND_DISPLAY is set and checks that it started. Built
against libxkbcommon 1.10 or newer, SDL required xkb_keymap_mod_get_mask()
(new in 1.10) at load time, so on Ubuntu 24.04 (libxkbcommon 1.6) the
driver reported itself unavailable.

xkb_keymapModifierLevels checks the masks the keymap handler computed,
through the SDL keymap they built: each level of a key is entered under
the SDL modifiers its xkb mask translates to, so a wrong shift, caps lock
or level 3 mask drops or misfiles the level. With FIZZY_TEST_XKB_LAYOUT=de
and a compositor keyboard on the German layout it checks Shift+2 = '"',
Caps+Q = 'Q', AltGr+Q = '@' and the like, and that no modifier is held.
Without the variable it is skipped.

fizzyedit/sdl_zig runs it under weston's X11 backend in Xvfb, on Ubuntu
24.04 and 26.04.

Part of fizzyedit/fizzy#280, for fizzyedit/fizzy#289.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
